From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] feat(editor): footnotes (پانویس) on selected text
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 2.3 (2026-10-16)  2.3: a click on an entry of the "Footnotes" list makes the
  whole footnoted text (not only its number) beat three times with the highlight color
  and a soft glow, and its number grows and shrinks with it (about 3 seconds, after the
  scroll). Without animation (reduced motion) the text is highlighted instead.
  2.2: the card shows the note text itself (no "Footnote 1"
  title); edit is beside it, close at the top and delete at the bottom, on the side of
  the interface language (Persian: edit right, close top left, delete bottom left;
  English mirrored). Footnote type in the dialog: automatic numbers (1, 2, 3),
  automatic letters (الف، ب، پ / a, b, c) or a custom label. Numbers and letters are
  two sequences without gaps: deleting a footnote renumbers the ones after it.
  2.1: a click on an entry of the "Footnotes" list (or on a
  reference) did nothing: the Mermaid plugin of code blocks, earlier in the plugin list,
  returns true for every click, so ProseMirror never called this plugin. The click is now
  listened to on the editor element directly; the entry moves to its reference in the
  text and flashes it (and a reference to its entry).
  2.0 = + cream/gray card, click on a list entry, mixed Persian/Latin notes (old 0021, 0022).
  Before: 1.0 (2026-10-14)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0013)

A footnote is attached to the selected text from a new button in the
selection (formatting) toolbar: "پانویس" in Persian, "Footnote" in English.
The button opens a dialog to write the note and, optionally, a custom label.

- Stored as a mark (footnote: id, label, note) on the selected text, so it
  is saved, synced and exported with the document; Markdown export writes it
  as an inline footnote text^[note].
- A superscript reference follows the marked text and every footnote is
  listed again in a "پانویس‌ها" / "Footnotes" section at the end of the
  document (decorations, not document content). Clicking a reference jumps
  to its entry and back; so does a click anywhere on an entry of the list.
- Numbering is automatic in document order. In a right-to-left block the
  number and the entry are right-to-left with Persian digits; in a
  left-to-right block left-to-right with Latin digits.
- The label is editable: a number, a letter or short text; empty means
  automatic. Digits in a custom label also follow the direction.
- Hovering the marked text, the reference or the list entry shows a tooltip
  with the note on a cream (light theme) or gray (dark theme) card. It closes when the pointer moves away, with Escape,
  on scroll, or with its close button. Edit and delete buttons are shown when
  the document is editable; the dialog also has a delete button.
- Deleting a footnote removes only the mark; the text stays. Pasted copies
  of footnoted text get new ids.

Card colors and click on an entry (was 0021 v1.0):
1. The footnote card (shown on hover) was dark navy in both themes. Now it is
   cream (#FFF8E6) in the light theme and gray (#3A3D44) in the dark theme, with
   the normal text color and a thin border.
2. In the "Footnotes" list at the end of the page, a click anywhere on an
   entry (not only on its number) moves to the footnote in the text and
   flashes it. The whole entry shows the pointing-hand cursor. A click that
   ends a text selection made inside the entry does not jump, so the note text
   can still be selected and copied.

Mixed Persian and Latin text (was 0022 v1.0):
Problem: the text of a footnote (in the list at the end, in the hover card and
in the edit form) used dir="auto", which takes the first strong letter. A
Persian note that starts with a Latin word (e.g. "Outline یک ابزار است") was
laid out left-to-right, and its Persian part and punctuation were scrambled.

Fix: new getMixedTextDirection(text, fallback) in shared/utils/rtl.ts:
  - only Persian/Arabic/Hebrew letters -> rtl
  - only Latin (and other LTR) letters  -> ltr
  - both kinds                          -> the direction of the block that
                                           holds the footnote (explicit
                                           direction of the paragraph, or
                                           detected as before)
Used for the note in the list, the card and the edit field (which follows the
text as it is typed). The note is also isolated (unicode-bidi: isolate) so the
number next to it cannot change its order.

